{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1438801-2e-maeljim-appereance","id":1438801,"title":"2E Maeljim Appereance.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-03-09T13:57:54-08:00","id":1438801,"title":"2E Maeljim Appereance.","content":"How do you imagine the 2e Maeljin look like if/when they can manifest a physical body?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T18:29:53-08:00","id":1438857,"title":"","content":"I think it would really be a matter of Claiming someone and making a horrible synthesis of flesh and spirit, so it depends on the host. Spirits vary in their appearance, even with the same spirit at different times yet symbolism must remain consistent. <br /> <br /> Pointing out the variables doesn't change the fact that I don't personally know, we could observe how they look in first edition and guess from there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T23:10:22-08:00","id":1438896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1438801-2e-maeljim-appereance#post1438801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you imagine the 2e Maeljin look like if/when they can manifest a physical body?</div> </div> </div> </div>Since you\u2019re talking 2e, they don\u2019t manifest physically. There\u2019s not much beyond Soulless Wolf\u2019s word they they even exist and it\u2019s not some kind of further trick from the darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T02:13:15-08:00","id":1438910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1438801-2e-maeljim-appereance?p=1438896#post1438896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Since you\u2019re talking 2e, they don\u2019t manifest physically. There\u2019s not much beyond Soulless Wolf\u2019s word they they even exist and it\u2019s not some kind of further trick from the darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting to know! Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T02:28:35-08:00","id":1438912,"title":"","content":"No problem. The Bale Hounds still have their dark, subversive powers and sell themselves to what they\u2019re told are the Maeljin. Maeltinet still exist and will say the Maeljin exist. But there\u2019s no objective proof of the claims. It could be true, it could all be smoke and mirrors, or it could be something much worse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T02:45:08-08:00","id":1438914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1438801-2e-maeljim-appereance?p=1438912#post1438912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No problem. The Bale Hounds still have their dark, subversive powers and sell themselves to what they\u2019re told are the Maeljin. Maeltinet still exist and will say the Maeljin exist. But there\u2019s no objective proof of the claims. It could be true, it could all be smoke and mirrors, or it could be something much worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>since Forsaken is a horror game,i can imagine any of those being true in a given person's game","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T00:24:13-07:00","id":1440555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1438801-2e-maeljim-appereance?p=1438912#post1438912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No problem. The Bale Hounds still have their dark, subversive powers and sell themselves to what they\u2019re told are the Maeljin. Maeltinet still exist and will say the Maeljin exist. But there\u2019s no objective proof of the claims. It could be true, it could all be smoke and mirrors, or it could be something much worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that Bale Hounds draw on some rather distinctive powers, the lie would have to be more elaborate than mere words.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T00:44:28-07:00","id":1440560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1438801-2e-maeljim-appereance?p=1440555#post1440555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given that Bale Hounds draw on some rather distinctive powers, the lie would have to be more elaborate than mere words.</div> </div> </div> </div>The lie is whether or not the Maeljin exist. There\u2019s no question that Soulless Wolf exists, only the extent of its powers and deceptiveness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-22T21:26:13-07:00","id":1441021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1438801-2e-maeljim-appereance?p=1440560#post1440560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The lie is whether or not the Maeljin exist. There\u2019s no question that Soulless Wolf exists, only the extent of its powers and deceptiveness.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, I am just saying that if Soulless Wolf made up the Maeljin then he would have to provide for all the distinctive powers somehow, perhaps collaborate with the the right Maeltinet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T02:23:40-07:00","id":1441045,"title":"","content":"Or that Soulless Wolf is just really weird and powerful? Who knows- maybe there aren't any Maeljin around because he eats them whenever the finds them, and the rest lay down hiding from him, and the boons the Maeljin grant only come from those he devoured.<br /> <br /> Like, Soulless Wolf questions a certain would be Bale Hound about what kinds of sins they like, and says &quot;I know just the guy for you, wait here&quot; and then goes out, searching after the right Maeljin, eats them, returns and says &quot;So we discussed it thoroughly and it seems that he agrees to the pact. Oh, the blood on my mouth? never mind that. So what do you say?&quot;<br /> <br /> Kind of a parody of the Sacred Hunt, in a way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T17:33:44-07:00","id":1441168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1438801-2e-maeljim-appereance?p=1441045#post1441045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or that Soulless Wolf is just really weird and powerful? Who knows- maybe there aren't any Maeljin around because he eats them whenever the finds them, and the rest lay down hiding from him, and the boons the Maeljin grant only come from those he devoured.<br /> <br /> Like, Soulless Wolf questions a certain would be Bale Hound about what kinds of sins they like, and says &amp;quot;I know just the guy for you, wait here&amp;quot; and then goes out, searching after the right Maeljin, eats them, returns and says &amp;quot;So we discussed it thoroughly and it seems that he agrees to the pact. Oh, the blood on my mouth? never mind that. So what do you say?&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Kind of a parody of the Sacred Hunt, in a way.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that was how it went, he finished off the common Maeljin long ago and doesn't need to hunt during every initiation. I suppose time turns everything to routine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-26T10:36:51-07:00","id":1441525,"title":"","content":"I would say that Soulless Wolf Equates to one of the Triatic Wyrms, and his Maeljin \u201cMasters\u201d would be the Urge Wyrms<br /> <br /> To use an Apocalypse Analogy. My take away is that there are no \u201cMaeljin\u201d per say - rather they are all split personalities of Soulless Wolf that are Quasi spirits in their own right","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}